title: 'Founder directive: stringent Paradigm symbols throughout the Gnomon build'
summary: |-
  The founder asked that the Gnomon build be stringent about Paradigm symbols, so the map of features and functionality stays easy to keep and update. Rules:
  - every new component, flow, gate, signal or aspect gets its .purpose entry in the same change;
  - the spec's Appendix A node ids are reused verbatim in .purpose files, code headers and commit Symbols trailers;
  - `paradigm purpose validate` and `paradigm index` run before every commit.

  The running PR-3 and PR-5 builders were told. It is saved as a feedback memory so every builder prompt carries it. Proposed enforcement: a gnomon test that cross-checks spec Appendix A nodes against .purpose symbols for implemented code, so drift fails CI.
